<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Repton</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Repton is a village in south <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derbyshire">Derbyshire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-trent">River Trent</a>. It was a royal centre of Mercia, with a double monastery whose church crypt became the burial place of kings, among them Æthelbald and Wiglaf. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-heathen-army">Great Heathen Army</a> wintered there in 873–874, and excavations have found its defended camp and a mass burial. The crypt survives beneath St Wystan's Church.</p></div>
